# Core vs Campaign assembly boundaries

Authority: [core assembly improvement plan](../docs/plans/core-assembly-improvement-plan.md), [05-class-design](../docs/05-class-design.md), [ADR 025](../decisions/025-campaign-exploration-target.md), [story-events](../docs/02-systems/story-events.md).

## Dependency (locked)

```
GridDungeon.Campaign  →  GridDungeon.Core   (only)
GridDungeon.Runtime   →  Core + Campaign
GridDungeon.Core      →  (none — never references Campaign)
```

`GridDungeon.Campaign.asmdef`: `noEngineReferences: true` (same as Core).

## Core owns (generic engine)

| Put in `Assets/Scripts/Core/` | Examples |
|--------------------------------|----------|
| Simulators / formulas | `DamageCalculator`, `MapRevealCalculator`, `TurnQueueBuilder` |
| Neutral models & DTOs | `ExplorationTarget`, `FloorExitLink`, `CombatEntryContext` |
| Story **data shapes** only | `StoryEventDefinitionData`, `StoryEventEffectData`, `StoryEventStepData` |
| Save schema | `SaveGame`, `CampaignSaveData`, `CampaignFlagAccessor` |
| Generic hub rules | `GuildPartyRules.IsPartyFormationReady` (slot count — no campaign flag writes) |

## Campaign owns (content / stratum behavior)

| Put in `Assets/Scripts/Campaign/` | Examples |
|-----------------------------------|----------|
| Stratum resolvers & constants | `S1CampaignResolver`, `S1FloorKeys`, `S1FloorExitLinks` |
| Story **execution** | `StoryEventEffectExecutor`, `StoryEventPlayOnceRules`, `StoryEventPlayback` |
| Content IDs & trigger catalogs | `StoryEventIds`, `StoryEventTriggerCatalog` |
| Tutorial / transition policy | `CombatTutorialHudRules`, `CampaignTransitionEffects`, `S1GuildPartyRules` |
| New-game bootstrap | `S1CampaignBootstrap` |

S2+ policy: `Campaign/S2/` (or sibling types) — do not grow `S1CampaignResolver` for unrelated acts.

## Do not add to Core

| Smell | Put instead |
|-------|-------------|
| `switch (storyEventId)` or per-event hardcoded effects | `StoryEventDefinition` asset effects + `StoryEventEffectExecutor` (Campaign) |
| S1 floor keys, spawn cells, encounter suppress in resolver | `S1CampaignResolver` or `Campaign/S2/*` |
| `RefreshPartyReadyFlag` / writing `campaign.S1*` from hub rules | `S1GuildPartyRules` (Campaign) |
| Tutorial encounter skip wired inside Core calculators | Campaign helper; Core takes `bool skipRewards` or predicate from Runtime |
| Hardcoded exploration trigger cells / prereq flags | `StoryEventTriggerCatalog` or floor asset rows ([#112](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/issues/112)) |
| `MonoBehaviour`, `UnityEngine`, ScriptableObject types | Runtime / Editor |

## PR / agent checklist

Before adding C# under `Core/`:

1. **Stratum- or story-specific?** → `Campaign/` (not Core).
2. **Only a data shape** crossing layers? → DTO in Core; behavior in Campaign or Runtime.
3. **Would a second stratum duplicate this with different constants?** → Campaign policy, not Core simulator.
4. **Does Core need a Campaign type?** → Stop — refactor (neutral DTO in Core, policy in Campaign). **Never** add `GridDungeon.Campaign` to `GridDungeon.Core.asmdef`.

## Tests

- Core simulator tests: `using GridDungeon.Core.*` only when testing generic rules.
- Campaign policy tests: `Tests/GameFlow/` — reference `GridDungeon.Campaign` (see `S1CampaignResolverTests`, `StoryEventRunnerTests`).
